{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013BTMJWoZ4GKDKnzPu4S2wT","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me create a detailed summary report.\n\n## Comprehensive Codebase Analysis: Roundnet Spain\n\n### 1. PROJECT STRUCTURE & TECH STACK\n\n**Framework & Core:**\n- **Next.js 16.1.6** - React framework with App Router (using new `[locale]` dynamic routing)\n- **React 19.2.3** - Latest React version with server components\n- **TypeScript 5** - Full type safety\n- **pnpm** - Package manager (monorepo ready with pnpm-workspace.yaml)\n\n**Key Dependencies:**\n```json\n{\n  \"@supabase/supabase-js\": \"^2.93.3\",\n  \"next-intl\": \"^4.8.2\",\n  \"class-variance-authority\": \"^0.7.1\",\n  \"clsx\": \"^2.1.1\",\n  \"lucide-react\": \"^0.563.0\",\n  \"radix-ui\": \"^1.4.3\",\n  \"tailwindcss\": \"^4\",\n  \"tailwind-merge\": \"^3.4.0\"\n}\n```\n\n**Directory Structure:**\n```\n/roundnet\n├── src/\n│   ├── app/[locale]/          # App Router with locale-based routing\n│   │   ├── layout.tsx         # Root layout with i18n client provider\n│   │   └── page.tsx           # Home page\n│   ├── components/            # React components (currently 3)\n│   │   ├── header.tsx         # Navigation header with mobile menu\n│   │   ├── footer.tsx         # Footer with links\n│   │   └── language-switcher.tsx # Language toggle (EN/ES)\n│   ├── lib/\n│   │   ├── supabase.ts        # Supabase client singleton\n│   │   └── utils.ts           # cn() utility for className merging\n│   ├── i18n/\n│   │   ├── config.ts          # Locale config (es, en with default es)\n│   │   ├── routing.ts         # next-intl routing config\n│   │   └── request.ts         # Server-side i18n request handler\n│   ├── middleware.ts          # next-intl middleware for routing\n│   └── api/health/route.ts    # Health check endpoint\n├── messages/                  # Translation files\n│   ├── en.json               # English translations\n│   └── es.json               # Spanish translations\n├── components.json           # shadcn/ui config\n├── next.config.ts            # Next.js config with i18n plugin\n├── tsconfig.json             # TypeScript config with @ alias\n├── postcss.config.mjs        # Tailwind PostCSS config\n└── .env.example              # Environment template\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. INTERNATIONALIZATION (i18n) - US-003 Implementation\n\n**Configuration:**\n- **Library:** `next-intl` v4.8.2\n- **Locales:** Spanish (es - default) and English (en)\n- **Setup:** Middleware-based routing with locale prefix in URL\n\n**Key Files:**\n\n**src/i18n/config.ts:**\n```typescript\nexport const locales = ['es', 'en'] as const;\nexport const defaultLocale = 'es' as const;\nexport type Locale = (typeof locales)[number];\n```\n\n**src/i18n/routing.ts:**\n```typescript\nexport const routing = defineRouting({\n  locales,\n  defaultLocale,\n});\n```\n\n**src/i18n/request.ts:**\n- Server-side config that loads messages based on locale\n- Returns locale + message bundle dynamically imported from `/messages/{locale}.json`\n\n**src/middleware.ts:**\n- Uses `createMiddleware` from next-intl\n- Intercepts all routes except `/api`, `/_next`, `/_vercel` and static files\n- Handles locale routing and redirects\n\n**Usage Pattern:**\n- Server Components: `getMessages()`, `setRequestLocale()`\n- Client Components: `useTranslations()`, `useLocale()`\n- URL structure: `/{locale}/path` (e.g., `/es/educational`, `/en/tournaments`)\n\n**Translation Structure:**\n```json\n{\n  \"common\": { \"language\", \"spanish\", \"english\" },\n  \"nav\": { \"home\", \"educational\", \"tournaments\", \"training\", \"rankings\", \"bulkOrders\", \"menu\", \"closeMenu\" },\n  \"auth\": { \"login\", \"logout\", \"profile\", \"account\" },\n  \"footer\": { \"rights\", \"privacy\", \"terms\", \"contact\" },\n  \"home\": { \"title\", \"description\", \"deployNow\", \"documentation\" },\n  \"metadata\": { \"title\", \"description\" }\n}\n```\n\n**Rich Text Support:**\n- Example in home page using `t.rich(\"description\", { templates, learning })` with custom renderers\n\n---\n\n### 3. AUTHENTICATION SETUP - Current State\n\n**Supabase Configuration:**\n```typescript\n// src/lib/supabase.ts\nimport { createClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js'\n\nconst supabaseUrl = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL\nconst supabaseAnonKey = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY\n\nif (!supabaseUrl || !supabaseAnonKey) {\n  throw new Error('Missing Supabase environment variables')\n}\n\nexport const supabase = createClient(supabaseUrl, supabaseAnonKey)\n```\n\n**Environment Variables (.env.example):**\n```\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your-supabase-url\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key\n```\n\n**Current Auth Status in Header:**\n```typescript\n// TODO: Replace with actual auth state from Supabase\nconst isAuthenticated = false;\n```\n\n**Health Check API (src/app/api/health/route.ts):**\n- Tests Supabase connection via `supabase.from('_health_check').select()`\n- Gracefully handles \"relation does not exist\" error\n- Returns status + timestamp\n\n**Not Yet Implemented:**\n- User authentication flows\n- Session management\n- Protected routes\n- Auth context/provider\n- Supabase auth helpers\n\n---\n\n### 4. BASE LAYOUT & NAVIGATION - US-004 Implementation\n\n**Root Layout (src/app/[locale]/layout.tsx):**\n```typescript\n- Uses async params with Promise<{ locale: string }>\n- Generates static params for all locales\n- Wraps children with NextIntlClientProvider\n- Applies Geist fonts (sans & mono)\n- 3-part layout: Header → Main → Footer\n- Validates locale and returns notFound() if invalid\n```\n\n**Navigation Structure:**\n```typescript\nconst navItems = [\n  { key: \"educational\", href: \"/educational\" },\n  { key: \"tournaments\", href: \"/tournaments\" },\n  { key: \"training\", href: \"/training\" },\n  { key: \"rankings\", href: \"/rankings\" },\n  { key: \"bulkOrders\", href: \"/bulk-orders\" },\n]\n```\n\n**Header Component (src/components/header.tsx):**\n- **Desktop Navigation:** Horizontal menu with all nav items\n- **Mobile Navigation:** Collapsible menu with smooth transitions\n- **Auth Integration:** Conditional rendering based on `isAuthenticated`\n  - Authenticated: Profile link with User icon\n  - Not authenticated: Login button with LogIn icon\n- **Language Switcher:** Inline component in both desktop and mobile\n- **Brand:** \"Roundnet Spain\" logo/title linking to home\n\n**Features:**\n- Sticky positioning with backdrop blur\n- Uses Lucide React icons (Menu, X, User, LogIn)\n- Responsive design using Tailwind (hidden md:flex patterns)\n- Mobile menu animation with transition-all and max-h transitions\n- Internationalized labels using useTranslations()\n\n**Footer Component (src/components/footer.tsx):**\n- 3-column grid (responsive to 1 column on mobile)\n- **Brand Section:** Logo + description\n- **Navigation Links:** All main nav items\n- **Legal Links:** Privacy, Terms, Contact\n- **Copyright:** Auto-updated year display\n\n**Language Switcher (src/components/language-switcher.tsx):**\n```typescript\n// Client component\n- Buttons for each locale\n- Active state styling (inverted colors)\n- Replaces locale prefix in URL pathname\n- Uses useLocale(), useRouter(), usePathname() hooks\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. STYLING & UI PATTERNS\n\n**Design System:**\n- **CSS Framework:** Tailwind CSS 4 with PostCSS integration\n- **Design Library:** shadcn/ui (configured but no components installed yet)\n- **Icon Library:** Lucide React\n\n**Configuration Files:**\n- **components.json:** shadcn/ui setup with:\n  - Style: \"new-york\"\n  - Tailwind base color: \"neutral\"\n  - Icon library: lucide\n  - Aliases: @/components, @/utils, @/ui, @/lib, @/hooks\n\n**Theme System (src/app/globals.css):**\n- CSS variables for light/dark mode\n- OKLCH color space (modern color system)\n- Dark mode class-based: `.dark { --variable: value }`\n- Variables: background, foreground, primary, secondary, muted, accent, destructive, border, input, ring, chart colors\n- Border radius scale: sm, md, lg, xl, 2xl, 3xl, 4xl\n\n**Utility Functions:**\n```typescript\n// src/lib/utils.ts\nexport function cn(...inputs: ClassValue[]) {\n  return twMerge(clsx(inputs))\n}\n// Combines clsx (conditional classnames) with tailwind-merge (conflict resolution)\n```\n\n**Tailwind Features:**\n- @import tw-animate-css for animations\n- @layer base for global styles\n- Responsive utilities (md: breakpoint patterns)\n- Custom @custom-variant for dark mode\n\n---\n\n### 6. FORM & VALIDATION PATTERNS - Currently Not Implemented\n\n**Current State:**\n- No form components or libraries present\n- No validation library (zod, react-hook-form, etc.)\n- No form-related hooks\n\n**Recommended Patterns to Implement:**\n- shadcn/ui form components (once added via CLI)\n- react-hook-form for form state management\n- zod for schema validation\n- Supabase form submission to tables\n\n---\n\n### 7. COMPONENT PATTERNS & BEST PRACTICES\n\n**Established Patterns:**\n\n1. **Server vs. Client Components:**\n   - Layout: Server component with async params\n   - Header/Footer: Client components (marked with \"use client\")\n   - Language Switcher: Client component\n   - Home page: Hybrid (async wrapper + client content component)\n\n2. **Styling Pattern:**\n   ```typescript\n   className={cn(\n     \"base-classes\",\n     condition && \"conditional-classes\",\n     someState ? \"state-true\" : \"state-false\"\n   )}\n   ```\n\n3. **Internationalization Usage:**\n   - Server: `getMessages()`, `setRequestLocale(locale)`\n   - Client: `useTranslations(\"namespace\")`, `useLocale()`\n   - Rich text with custom renderers\n\n4. **Link Navigation:**\n   - Always locale-aware: `href={`/${locale}/path`}`\n   - Uses next/link and next/navigation\n\n5. **State Management:**\n   - useState for simple UI state (mobile menu open/close)\n   - No global state management yet (Redux/Zustand/Context)\n\n---\n\n### 8. SUPABASE CLIENT USAGE\n\n**Singleton Pattern:**\n```typescript\n// src/lib/supabase.ts\nexport const supabase = createClient(supabaseUrl, supabaseAnonKey)\n```\n\n**Usage Examples:**\n- Health check: `supabase.from('table').select()`\n- Ready for: auth, database queries, real-time subscriptions\n\n**Notes:**\n- Using public anon key (NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix)\n- No Server-side (service role) key setup yet\n- No RLS (Row Level Security) policies documented\n- No database schema currently queried except health check\n\n---\n\n### 9. KEY TAKEAWAYS & PATTERNS TO FOLLOW\n\n**When Adding New Features:**\n\n1. **Forms:**\n   - Use react-hook-form + zod + shadcn/ui\n   - Pattern: `useForm()` hook with `handleSubmit()` pattern\n   - Validation: Zod schemas for client + server validation\n\n2. **Database:**\n   - Query pattern: `const { data, error } = await supabase.from('table').select()`\n   - Always check error: `if (error) { /* handle */ }`\n   - For mutations: `.insert()`, `.update()`, `.delete()` methods\n\n3. **Internationalization:**\n   - Always access locale via `useLocale()` (client) or params (server)\n   - Build URLs as: `/${locale}/path`\n   - Namespace translations logically in JSON structure\n\n4. **Styling:**\n   - Use `cn()` utility for dynamic className merging\n   - Leverage Tailwind responsive classes and dark mode\n   - Follow design system variables in globals.css\n\n5. **Routing:**\n   - All routes must respect `[locale]` parameter\n   - Use Link component with locale prefix\n   - Middleware handles locale validation\n\n6. **Components:**\n   - Mark interactive components with \"use client\"\n   - Use TypeScript for prop types\n   - Keep server/client concerns separated\n\n---\n\n### 10. ENVIRONMENT SETUP\n\n**Required .env.local:**\n```\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=<your-project-url>\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<your-anon-key>\n```\n\n**Scripts:**\n- `npm run dev` - Development server\n- `npm run build` - Production build\n- `npm run start` - Production start\n- `npm run lint` - ESLint check\n- `npm run typecheck` - TypeScript check\n\n---\n\n### 11. CURRENT GAPS & TODO ITEMS\n\n1. **Authentication System:**\n   - Supabase Auth integration (signup, login, logout, session)\n   - Auth context/provider for component access\n   - Protected routes\n   - User profile pages\n\n2. **Form Components:**\n   - Add shadcn/ui components via CLI\n   - Implement form with validation\n   - Error handling and submission states\n\n3. **Database Integration:**\n   - Schema definition for tournaments, users, rankings, etc.\n   - CRUD operations for main entities\n   - Real-time subscriptions if needed\n\n4. **Error Handling:**\n   - Global error boundaries\n   - Toast/notification system\n   - User-friendly error messages\n\n5. **Testing:**\n   - No test configuration present\n   - Would recommend: Vitest + React Testing Library\n\n6. **Content Pages:**\n   - /educational, /tournaments, /training, /rankings, /bulk-orders pages not yet created\n\nThis is a well-structured Next.js 16 project with modern tooling, internationalization support, and Supabase integration foundation ready for expansion into a full-featured Roundnet Spain federation platform."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a0f55ba (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b462f71f-cc96-4f44-b5a7-de6841443bc4","uuid":"e71e4da5-b215-4c40-b08f-5b4550e3ce8d","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the codebase to understand:\n1. The project structure and tech stack (looks like it might be Next.js with Supabase based on git history)\n2. Existing authentication setup if any\n3. How internationalization is implemented (US-003 was about i18n)\n4. The base layout and navigation patterns (US-004)\n5. Existing form patterns or UI components being used\n6. Supabase configuration\n\nFocus on understanding patterns for:\n- Form handling and validation\n- Supabase client usage\n- Translation/i18n usage\n- Component structure\n\nProvide a thorough summary of what you find.","agentId":"a0f55ba","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me create a detailed summary report.\n\n## Comprehensive Codebase Analysis: Roundnet Spain\n\n### 1. PROJECT STRUCTURE & TECH STACK\n\n**Framework & Core:**\n- **Next.js 16.1.6** - React framework with App Router (using new `[locale]` dynamic routing)\n- **React 19.2.3** - Latest React version with server components\n- **TypeScript 5** - Full type safety\n- **pnpm** - Package manager (monorepo ready with pnpm-workspace.yaml)\n\n**Key Dependencies:**\n```json\n{\n  \"@supabase/supabase-js\": \"^2.93.3\",\n  \"next-intl\": \"^4.8.2\",\n  \"class-variance-authority\": \"^0.7.1\",\n  \"clsx\": \"^2.1.1\",\n  \"lucide-react\": \"^0.563.0\",\n  \"radix-ui\": \"^1.4.3\",\n  \"tailwindcss\": \"^4\",\n  \"tailwind-merge\": \"^3.4.0\"\n}\n```\n\n**Directory Structure:**\n```\n/roundnet\n├── src/\n│   ├── app/[locale]/          # App Router with locale-based routing\n│   │   ├── layout.tsx         # Root layout with i18n client provider\n│   │   └── page.tsx           # Home page\n│   ├── components/            # React components (currently 3)\n│   │   ├── header.tsx         # Navigation header with mobile menu\n│   │   ├── footer.tsx         # Footer with links\n│   │   └── language-switcher.tsx # Language toggle (EN/ES)\n│   ├── lib/\n│   │   ├── supabase.ts        # Supabase client singleton\n│   │   └── utils.ts           # cn() utility for className merging\n│   ├── i18n/\n│   │   ├── config.ts          # Locale config (es, en with default es)\n│   │   ├── routing.ts         # next-intl routing config\n│   │   └── request.ts         # Server-side i18n request handler\n│   ├── middleware.ts          # next-intl middleware for routing\n│   └── api/health/route.ts    # Health check endpoint\n├── messages/                  # Translation files\n│   ├── en.json               # English translations\n│   └── es.json               # Spanish translations\n├── components.json           # shadcn/ui config\n├── next.config.ts            # Next.js config with i18n plugin\n├── tsconfig.json             # TypeScript config with @ alias\n├── postcss.config.mjs        # Tailwind PostCSS config\n└── .env.example              # Environment template\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. INTERNATIONALIZATION (i18n) - US-003 Implementation\n\n**Configuration:**\n- **Library:** `next-intl` v4.8.2\n- **Locales:** Spanish (es - default) and English (en)\n- **Setup:** Middleware-based routing with locale prefix in URL\n\n**Key Files:**\n\n**src/i18n/config.ts:**\n```typescript\nexport const locales = ['es', 'en'] as const;\nexport const defaultLocale = 'es' as const;\nexport type Locale = (typeof locales)[number];\n```\n\n**src/i18n/routing.ts:**\n```typescript\nexport const routing = defineRouting({\n  locales,\n  defaultLocale,\n});\n```\n\n**src/i18n/request.ts:**\n- Server-side config that loads messages based on locale\n- Returns locale + message bundle dynamically imported from `/messages/{locale}.json`\n\n**src/middleware.ts:**\n- Uses `createMiddleware` from next-intl\n- Intercepts all routes except `/api`, `/_next`, `/_vercel` and static files\n- Handles locale routing and redirects\n\n**Usage Pattern:**\n- Server Components: `getMessages()`, `setRequestLocale()`\n- Client Components: `useTranslations()`, `useLocale()`\n- URL structure: `/{locale}/path` (e.g., `/es/educational`, `/en/tournaments`)\n\n**Translation Structure:**\n```json\n{\n  \"common\": { \"language\", \"spanish\", \"english\" },\n  \"nav\": { \"home\", \"educational\", \"tournaments\", \"training\", \"rankings\", \"bulkOrders\", \"menu\", \"closeMenu\" },\n  \"auth\": { \"login\", \"logout\", \"profile\", \"account\" },\n  \"footer\": { \"rights\", \"privacy\", \"terms\", \"contact\" },\n  \"home\": { \"title\", \"description\", \"deployNow\", \"documentation\" },\n  \"metadata\": { \"title\", \"description\" }\n}\n```\n\n**Rich Text Support:**\n- Example in home page using `t.rich(\"description\", { templates, learning })` with custom renderers\n\n---\n\n### 3. AUTHENTICATION SETUP - Current State\n\n**Supabase Configuration:**\n```typescript\n// src/lib/supabase.ts\nimport { createClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js'\n\nconst supabaseUrl = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL\nconst supabaseAnonKey = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY\n\nif (!supabaseUrl || !supabaseAnonKey) {\n  throw new Error('Missing Supabase environment variables')\n}\n\nexport const supabase = createClient(supabaseUrl, supabaseAnonKey)\n```\n\n**Environment Variables (.env.example):**\n```\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your-supabase-url\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key\n```\n\n**Current Auth Status in Header:**\n```typescript\n// TODO: Replace with actual auth state from Supabase\nconst isAuthenticated = false;\n```\n\n**Health Check API (src/app/api/health/route.ts):**\n- Tests Supabase connection via `supabase.from('_health_check').select()`\n- Gracefully handles \"relation does not exist\" error\n- Returns status + timestamp\n\n**Not Yet Implemented:**\n- User authentication flows\n- Session management\n- Protected routes\n- Auth context/provider\n- Supabase auth helpers\n\n---\n\n### 4. BASE LAYOUT & NAVIGATION - US-004 Implementation\n\n**Root Layout (src/app/[locale]/layout.tsx):**\n```typescript\n- Uses async params with Promise<{ locale: string }>\n- Generates static params for all locales\n- Wraps children with NextIntlClientProvider\n- Applies Geist fonts (sans & mono)\n- 3-part layout: Header → Main → Footer\n- Validates locale and returns notFound() if invalid\n```\n\n**Navigation Structure:**\n```typescript\nconst navItems = [\n  { key: \"educational\", href: \"/educational\" },\n  { key: \"tournaments\", href: \"/tournaments\" },\n  { key: \"training\", href: \"/training\" },\n  { key: \"rankings\", href: \"/rankings\" },\n  { key: \"bulkOrders\", href: \"/bulk-orders\" },\n]\n```\n\n**Header Component (src/components/header.tsx):**\n- **Desktop Navigation:** Horizontal menu with all nav items\n- **Mobile Navigation:** Collapsible menu with smooth transitions\n- **Auth Integration:** Conditional rendering based on `isAuthenticated`\n  - Authenticated: Profile link with User icon\n  - Not authenticated: Login button with LogIn icon\n- **Language Switcher:** Inline component in both desktop and mobile\n- **Brand:** \"Roundnet Spain\" logo/title linking to home\n\n**Features:**\n- Sticky positioning with backdrop blur\n- Uses Lucide React icons (Menu, X, User, LogIn)\n- Responsive design using Tailwind (hidden md:flex patterns)\n- Mobile menu animation with transition-all and max-h transitions\n- Internationalized labels using useTranslations()\n\n**Footer Component (src/components/footer.tsx):**\n- 3-column grid (responsive to 1 column on mobile)\n- **Brand Section:** Logo + description\n- **Navigation Links:** All main nav items\n- **Legal Links:** Privacy, Terms, Contact\n- **Copyright:** Auto-updated year display\n\n**Language Switcher (src/components/language-switcher.tsx):**\n```typescript\n// Client component\n- Buttons for each locale\n- Active state styling (inverted colors)\n- Replaces locale prefix in URL pathname\n- Uses useLocale(), useRouter(), usePathname() hooks\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. STYLING & UI PATTERNS\n\n**Design System:**\n- **CSS Framework:** Tailwind CSS 4 with PostCSS integration\n- **Design Library:** shadcn/ui (configured but no components installed yet)\n- **Icon Library:** Lucide React\n\n**Configuration Files:**\n- **components.json:** shadcn/ui setup with:\n  - Style: \"new-york\"\n  - Tailwind base color: \"neutral\"\n  - Icon library: lucide\n  - Aliases: @/components, @/utils, @/ui, @/lib, @/hooks\n\n**Theme System (src/app/globals.css):**\n- CSS variables for light/dark mode\n- OKLCH color space (modern color system)\n- Dark mode class-based: `.dark { --variable: value }`\n- Variables: background, foreground, primary, secondary, muted, accent, destructive, border, input, ring, chart colors\n- Border radius scale: sm, md, lg, xl, 2xl, 3xl, 4xl\n\n**Utility Functions:**\n```typescript\n// src/lib/utils.ts\nexport function cn(...inputs: ClassValue[]) {\n  return twMerge(clsx(inputs))\n}\n// Combines clsx (conditional classnames) with tailwind-merge (conflict resolution)\n```\n\n**Tailwind Features:**\n- @import tw-animate-css for animations\n- @layer base for global styles\n- Responsive utilities (md: breakpoint patterns)\n- Custom @custom-variant for dark mode\n\n---\n\n### 6. FORM & VALIDATION PATTERNS - Currently Not Implemented\n\n**Current State:**\n- No form components or libraries present\n- No validation library (zod, react-hook-form, etc.)\n- No form-related hooks\n\n**Recommended Patterns to Implement:**\n- shadcn/ui form components (once added via CLI)\n- react-hook-form for form state management\n- zod for schema validation\n- Supabase form submission to tables\n\n---\n\n### 7. COMPONENT PATTERNS & BEST PRACTICES\n\n**Established Patterns:**\n\n1. **Server vs. Client Components:**\n   - Layout: Server component with async params\n   - Header/Footer: Client components (marked with \"use client\")\n   - Language Switcher: Client component\n   - Home page: Hybrid (async wrapper + client content component)\n\n2. **Styling Pattern:**\n   ```typescript\n   className={cn(\n     \"base-classes\",\n     condition && \"conditional-classes\",\n     someState ? \"state-true\" : \"state-false\"\n   )}\n   ```\n\n3. **Internationalization Usage:**\n   - Server: `getMessages()`, `setRequestLocale(locale)`\n   - Client: `useTranslations(\"namespace\")`, `useLocale()`\n   - Rich text with custom renderers\n\n4. **Link Navigation:**\n   - Always locale-aware: `href={`/${locale}/path`}`\n   - Uses next/link and next/navigation\n\n5. **State Management:**\n   - useState for simple UI state (mobile menu open/close)\n   - No global state management yet (Redux/Zustand/Context)\n\n---\n\n### 8. SUPABASE CLIENT USAGE\n\n**Singleton Pattern:**\n```typescript\n// src/lib/supabase.ts\nexport const supabase = createClient(supabaseUrl, supabaseAnonKey)\n```\n\n**Usage Examples:**\n- Health check: `supabase.from('table').select()`\n- Ready for: auth, database queries, real-time subscriptions\n\n**Notes:**\n- Using public anon key (NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix)\n- No Server-side (service role) key setup yet\n- No RLS (Row Level Security) policies documented\n- No database schema currently queried except health check\n\n---\n\n### 9. KEY TAKEAWAYS & PATTERNS TO FOLLOW\n\n**When Adding New Features:**\n\n1. **Forms:**\n   - Use react-hook-form + zod + shadcn/ui\n   - Pattern: `useForm()` hook with `handleSubmit()` pattern\n   - Validation: Zod schemas for client + server validation\n\n2. **Database:**\n   - Query pattern: `const { data, error } = await supabase.from('table').select()`\n   - Always check error: `if (error) { /* handle */ }`\n   - For mutations: `.insert()`, `.update()`, `.delete()` methods\n\n3. **Internationalization:**\n   - Always access locale via `useLocale()` (client) or params (server)\n   - Build URLs as: `/${locale}/path`\n   - Namespace translations logically in JSON structure\n\n4. **Styling:**\n   - Use `cn()` utility for dynamic className merging\n   - Leverage Tailwind responsive classes and dark mode\n   - Follow design system variables in globals.css\n\n5. **Routing:**\n   - All routes must respect `[locale]` parameter\n   - Use Link component with locale prefix\n   - Middleware handles locale validation\n\n6. **Components:**\n   - Mark interactive components with \"use client\"\n   - Use TypeScript for prop types\n   - Keep server/client concerns separated\n\n---\n\n### 10. ENVIRONMENT SETUP\n\n**Required .env.local:**\n```\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=<your-project-url>\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<your-anon-key>\n```\n\n**Scripts:**\n- `npm run dev` - Development server\n- `npm run build` - Production build\n- `npm run start` - Production start\n- `npm run lint` - ESLint check\n- `npm run typecheck` - TypeScript check\n\n---\n\n### 11. CURRENT GAPS & TODO ITEMS\n\n1. **Authentication System:**\n   - Supabase Auth integration (signup, login, logout, session)\n   - Auth context/provider for component access\n   - Protected routes\n   - User profile pages\n\n2. **Form Components:**\n   - Add shadcn/ui components via CLI\n   - Implement form with validation\n   - Error handling and submission states\n\n3. **Database Integration:**\n   - Schema definition for tournaments, users, rankings, etc.\n   - CRUD operations for main entities\n   - Real-time subscriptions if needed\n\n4. **Error Handling:**\n   - Global error boundaries\n   - Toast/notification system\n   - User-friendly error messages\n\n5. **Testing:**\n   - No test configuration present\n   - Would recommend: Vitest + React Testing Library\n\n6. **Content Pages:**\n   - /educational, /tournaments, /training, /rankings, /bulk-orders pages not yet created\n\nThis is a well-structured Next.js 16 project with modern tooling, internationalization support, and Supabase integration foundation ready for expansion into a full-featured Roundnet Spain federation platform."}],"totalDurationMs":74618,"totalTokens":51875,"totalToolUseCount":34,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":417,"cache_read_input_tokens":51449,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":417},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"}}}
